<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Fenwick</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1603–1657</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Fenwick was an English Puritan lawyer and one of the patentees of the Saybrook Colony at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut-river">Connecticut River</a>. He lived at Saybrook as governor from 1639 and in 1644 sold the fort and its lands to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> Colony. He returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and served as a parliamentary officer and MP during the Civil War.</p></div>
